FastJEV inference source distribution

This distribution includes inference code from OmniJev.
Upstream project: https://github.com/tinnel123666888/OmniJev
Copyright 2026 Beijing Zhongguancun Academy, Institute of Automation of the
Chinese Academy of Sciences, and Zevo. The upstream LICENSE is retained.

FastJEV additions provide candidate prefix sharing, shared recurrent initial
states, omission of unused leaf recurrent caches, and candidate block pruning.
The mso/infer.py and mso/fast_kernels.py files include local changes made during
the FastJEV experiments. The fastjev package extracts the main experiment's
input/readout protocols and adds a portable, local-checkpoint inference entry.

mso/terminal_state_factorial.py contains code derived from the
flash-linear-attention project. Its MIT license and attribution are retained
in that file. https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention

No dataset examples, pretrained weights, evaluation predictions, or paper
figures are distributed. Checkpoint manifests contain public repository
revisions and checksums only. Model and dataset licenses apply separately.
